<title>UK: British business bankruptcies down in Q3 -D&amp;B.</title>
<headline>British business bankruptcies down in Q3 -D&amp;B.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Business information suppliers Dun &amp; Bradstreet released the following data on business bankruptcies in Britain on Monday.</p>
<p>			Q3 1996	  Q3 1995	 pct change</p>
<p> BANKRUPTCIES     9,694	    10,379	  -6.6</p>
<p> LIQUIDATIONS    13,695	    13,106	   4.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Philip Mellor, senior analyst at D&amp;B, said the largest falls were in London, the North West and Wales. &quot;The decline in business failures has spread from the capital to most parts of the country and this must be good news.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
